    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Index Nodes (inode) is a data structure that stores information about a file or directory, such as its size, permissions, ownership, and disk block addresses. Each file and directory on a filesystem has a unique inode number.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;</content>
